window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-3623d131a0f26273"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"triage-a-backlog\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">分流待处理发现项</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。如需查看文档的 Markdown 版本，可在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>。</p> </blockquote> <p>使用 <code>$codex-security:triage-finding</code>，根据当前代码仓库审核现有安全发现项。此工作流程只进行静态分析，不会更改代码：Codex 会将每个发现视为尚未证实的主张，并检查代码仓库证据，但不会执行代码。</p> <p>请在针对目标代码仓库配置的 Codex 项目中运行此工作流程。Codex 必须能够读取该仓库的源代码。Jira 和 Linear 连接器可以提供发现项数据；GitHub 发现项则需要已验证身份的 GitHub REST 访问权限。这些连接器和访问权限都不能替代对源代码本身的读取权限。</p> <p>这与 <code>$codex-security:validation</code> 不同。后者可以构建或运行代码、创建测试或概念验证，或操作真实界面来复现或证伪某项发现。使用分流流程对待处理发现项进行分类和排序；如果运行时证据可能解决静态证据留下的不确定性，则使用验证流程。</p> <p>待处理发现项分流以已有发现为起点。若要搜索代码仓库中的新漏洞，请<a href=\"#/article/a-52ffdad46ad27a2b\">运行安全扫描</a>。分流流程不会修改代码仓库，也不会实施修复。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-the-findings-to-triage\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">选择要分流的发现项</h2> <p>你可以提供以下任一来源的单个发现项或一组发现项：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>来源</th> <th>需要提供的内容</th> <th>要求</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>粘贴的内容或本地发现</td> <td>SARIF 结果、CVE 或 GHSA、安全公告、扫描器问题单、漏洞赏金报告、Codex Security 发现产物，或用自然语言描述的漏洞主张。</td> <td>不需要连接器。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Jira 或 Linear</td> <td>准确的安全或漏洞问题 URL/标识符、Jira JQL，或 Linear 团队、项目或搜索短语。Codex 会先检索所选问题的内容，再进行分流。</td> <td>需要通过 Atlassian Rovo 连接 Jira（已阻止不安全链接），或连接 Linear（已阻止不安全链接），并具有读取权限。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>GitHub</td> <td>一个代码仓库，以及一种发现来源：代码扫描、<code>Dependabot</code> 漏洞和恶意软件、安全公告和私密漏洞报告，或全部来源。如果未指定代码仓库，Codex 会在可用时使用当前 Codex 项目所关联的 GitHub 仓库。默认不包括 GitHub Issues；请提供具体问题，或明确要求包含 GitHub Issues。</td> <td>需要已验证身份的 GitHub REST 访问权限，例如 <code>gh auth token</code>、<code>GH_TOKEN</code> 或 <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code>，并具有读取所选仓库和发现类型的权限。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>每条输入发现都会在结果中保留一项记录，并维持原有顺序，以便追踪其来源。即使看起来重复，Codex 也不会合并或丢弃发现项。</p> <p><a id=\"run-read-only-triage\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">运行只读分流</h2> <p>对于粘贴的发现项或本地产物，可以发送类似这样的提示：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:triage-finding to triage these existing security findings against this repository:\n\n[Paste the findings or provide the artifact path.]\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">使用 $codex-security:triage-finding，结合这个代码仓库，对以下现有安全发现项进行分诊：\n\n[Paste the findings or provide the artifact path.]</div></div> <p>对于 Jira 或 Linear 问题，请明确指定问题集合，并保持源系统只读：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:triage-finding to import and triage the security findings from [Jira or Linear issue URLs, identifiers, or query] against this repository.\nDo not change the source issues.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">使用 $codex-security:triage-finding，从 [Jira or Linear issue URLs, identifiers, or query] 导入安全发现项，并结合这个代码仓库进行分诊。\n不要更改来源问题。</div></div> <p>对于 GitHub 发现项，请写明代码仓库和发现来源：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:triage-finding to import and triage [code scanning, Dependabot vulnerabilities and malware, security advisories and private vulnerability reports, or all] from [owner/repository] against this repository.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">使用 $codex-security:triage-finding，从 [owner/repository] 导入 [code scanning, Dependabot vulnerabilities and malware, security advisories and private vulnerability reports, or all]，并结合这个代码仓库进行分诊。</div></div> <p>若要使用当前 Codex 项目关联的 GitHub 代码仓库，只需指定发现来源：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:triage-finding to import and triage [code scanning, Dependabot vulnerabilities and malware, security advisories and private vulnerability reports, or all] from GitHub against this repository. Use the GitHub repository attached to the current Codex project.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">使用 $codex-security:triage-finding，从 GitHub 导入 [code scanning, Dependabot vulnerabilities and malware, security advisories and private vulnerability reports, or all]，并结合这个代码仓库进行分诊。使用附加到当前 Codex 项目的 GitHub 仓库。</div></div> <p>Codex 会检查当前源代码和适用的 <code>SECURITY.md</code> 策略，然后为每条输入发现返回一个判定，并同时记录支持和反对该主张的证据，以及尚未解决的问题。</p> <p><a id=\"review-the-results\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">查看结果</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>判定</th> <th>含义</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>confirmed</code></td> <td>代码仓库证据表明，在所述前提下可以访问存在漏洞的代码路径，并且该路径跨越了受支持的安全边界。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>not_actionable</code></td> <td>代码仓库证据排除了该主张，例如证明版本不受影响、路径不可达、保护措施有效，或相关代码不会随产品发布。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>needs_review</code></td> <td>代码仓库证据不足以作出判断，因为所需信息缺失、含糊，依赖运行时、环境或策略，或仍有其他不确定因素。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>可以使用排序结果，优先处理需要修复的 <code>confirmed</code> 项，以及需要进一步调查的 <code>needs_review</code> 项。每个分组会分别排序。</p> <p>在采取行动前，请结合受影响的代码和攻击者所需前提，阅读判定理由，并核对证据是否支持该主张以及仍有哪些问题未解决。这里的 <code>confirmed</code> 表示静态代码仓库证据支持该发现，并不表示已经通过执行程序复现。</p> <p>除非你在查看分流结果后要求 Codex 更新，否则 Jira、Linear 和其他待处理记录都不会发生改变。</p> <p><a id=\"next-steps\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">后续步骤</h2> <ul> <li><strong><code>confirmed</code>：</strong> 人工接受该发现并决定修复后，使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\"><code>$codex-security:fix-finding</code></a>进行修复和验证。分流流程只准备可直接用于后续工作的交接提示，不会自动调用该技能。</li> <li><strong><code>needs_review</code>：</strong> 如果运行代码可以弥补证据缺口，请使用 <code>$codex-security:validation</code> 对照运行中的代码测试该发现。传入发现主张、受影响位置、前提条件、静态证据和分流结果中的证据缺口：</li> </ul> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">  Use $codex-security:validation to dynamically validate finding [triage item ID or source ID] from the backlog triage result. Reproduce or disprove the finding, record what you tested, and list any remaining uncertainty.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">使用 $codex-security:validation，对待办分诊结果中的发现项 [triage item ID or source ID] 进行动态验证。复现或证伪该发现项，记录测试过什么，并列出任何尚存的不确定性。</div></div> <p>与分流不同，验证可能会构建或运行代码、创建测试或概念验证，或操作真实界面。有关执行控制，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">Codex 审批和安全策略</a>。</p> <ul> <li><strong><code>needs_review</code>：</strong> 如果发现取决于产品策略或部署环境，请先回答列出的问题，再修改代码。</li> <li><strong><code>not_actionable</code>：</strong> 将证据与分流记录一并保存。Codex 不会自动关闭或更新来源工单。</li> <li>若要查找输入待处理列表之外的漏洞，请<a href=\"#/article/a-52ffdad46ad27a2b\">运行安全扫描</a>。</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"triage-a-backlog\">Triage a backlog</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Use <code>$codex-security:triage-finding</code> to review existing security findings against the current repository. This workflow performs a read-only static analysis: Codex treats each finding as an unproven claim and inspects repository evidence without executing the code.</p> <p>Run this workflow from a Codex project scoped to the repository you want to assess. Codex must be able to read the repository's source code. Jira and Linear connectors can provide finding data, while GitHub findings require authenticated GitHub REST access. Neither replaces access to the source code.</p> <p>This differs from <code>$codex-security:validation</code>, which can build or run code, create a test or proof of concept, or exercise a real interface to reproduce or disprove a finding. Use triage to classify and rank an existing backlog. Use validation when runtime evidence could resolve a finding that static evidence leaves uncertain.</p> <p>Backlog triage starts from existing findings. To search the repository for new vulnerabilities, <a href=\"#/article/a-52ffdad46ad27a2b\">run a security scan</a>. Triage doesn't modify the repository or implement fixes.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-the-findings-to-triage\">Choose the findings to triage</h2> <p>You can supply one finding or a collection from these sources:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Source</th> <th>What to provide</th> <th>Requirements</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Pasted or local findings</td> <td>SARIF results, a CVE or GHSA, an advisory, a scanner ticket, a bug bounty report, a Codex Security finding artifact, or a plain-language vulnerability claim.</td> <td>No connector required.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Jira or Linear</td> <td>Exact security or vulnerability issue URLs or identifiers, Jira JQL, or a Linear team, project, or search phrase. Codex retrieves the selected issue content before triage.</td> <td>Jira through Atlassian Rovo (blocked unsafe link) or Linear (blocked unsafe link) with read access.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>GitHub</td> <td>A repository and one finding source: code scanning, <code>Dependabot</code> vulnerabilities and malware, security advisories and private vulnerability reports, or all sources. If you don't specify a repository, Codex uses the GitHub repository attached to the current Codex project when available. GitHub Issues aren't included by default. Provide a specific issue or ask for GitHub Issues explicitly.</td> <td>Authenticated GitHub REST access, such as <code>gh auth token</code>, <code>GH_TOKEN</code>, or <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code>, with permission to read the selected repository and finding type.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Codex keeps one result for every supplied finding, in input order, so each source finding stays traceable. It doesn't merge or drop findings that look like duplicates.</p> <h2 id=\"run-read-only-triage\">Run read-only triage</h2> <p>For pasted findings or local artifacts, send a prompt like:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:triage-finding to triage these existing security findings against this repository:\n\n[Paste the findings or provide the artifact path.]\n</code></pre> <p>For Jira or Linear issues, identify the issue set and keep the source system read-only:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:triage-finding to import and triage the security findings from [Jira or Linear issue URLs, identifiers, or query] against this repository.\nDo not change the source issues.\n</code></pre> <p>For GitHub findings, name the repository and source:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:triage-finding to import and triage [code scanning, Dependabot vulnerabilities and malware, security advisories and private vulnerability reports, or all] from [owner/repository] against this repository.\n</code></pre> <p>To use the GitHub repository attached to the current Codex project, specify only the finding source:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:triage-finding to import and triage [code scanning, Dependabot vulnerabilities and malware, security advisories and private vulnerability reports, or all] from GitHub against this repository. Use the GitHub repository attached to the current Codex project.\n</code></pre> <p>Codex checks the current source and applicable <code>SECURITY.md</code> policy, then returns a verdict for every input finding. It records evidence both for and against the claim, along with unresolved questions.</p> <h2 id=\"review-the-results\">Review the results</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Verdict</th> <th>What it means</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>confirmed</code></td> <td>Repository evidence shows that the vulnerable path is reachable under the stated preconditions and crosses a supported security boundary.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>not_actionable</code></td> <td>Repository evidence rules out the claim, such as by showing an unaffected version, unreachable path, effective guard, or non-shipped surface.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>needs_review</code></td> <td>Repository evidence isn't enough to decide because required information is missing, ambiguous, runtime-dependent, environment-dependent, or policy-dependent.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Use the rankings to decide which <code>confirmed</code> findings to fix first and which <code>needs_review</code> findings to investigate first. Each group is ranked separately.</p> <p>Read the verdict's rationale alongside the affected code and attacker prerequisites. Check the evidence against the claim and any open questions before acting on the rank. Here, <code>confirmed</code> means supported by static repository evidence, not reproduced by executing the application.</p> <p>Jira, Linear, and other backlog records remain unchanged unless you ask Codex to update them after reviewing the triage results.</p> <h2 id=\"next-steps\">Next steps</h2> <ul> <li><code>confirmed</code>: After a person accepts the finding for remediation, use <a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\"><code>$codex-security:fix-finding</code></a> to fix and verify it. Triage prepares a prompt-ready handoff but doesn't invoke the skill automatically.</li> <li><code>needs_review</code>: If running code can resolve the proof gap, use <code>$codex-security:validation</code> to test the finding against running code. Pass the finding claim, affected locations, preconditions, static evidence, and proof gaps from the triage result:</li> </ul> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">  Use $codex-security:validation to dynamically validate finding [triage item ID or source ID] from the backlog triage result. Reproduce or disprove the finding, record what you tested, and list any remaining uncertainty.\n</code></pre> <p>Unlike triage, validation may build or run code, create a test or proof of concept, or exercise a real interface. See <a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">Codex approval and security policies</a> for execution controls.</p> <ul> <li><code>needs_review</code>: If the finding depends on product policy or deployment context, answer the listed open questions before changing code.</li> <li><code>not_actionable</code>: Keep the evidence with your triage record. Codex doesn't automatically close or update the source ticket.</li> <li>To look for vulnerabilities beyond the supplied backlog, <a href=\"#/article/a-52ffdad46ad27a2b\">run a security scan</a>.</li> </ul>"};
